t is declared, which prevents the earlier access from updating when this value changes over time.\n\n/Users/alextian/Documents/Claude/Projects/AI Staff/amc-kanban/src/components/dashboard/DashboardHome.tsx:563:7\n  561 |       setBrandSettings(null)\n  562 |       setBrandAgents([])\n> 563 |       setDismissedIds(new Set())\n      |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `setDismissedIds` accessed before it is declared\n  564 |       setAutoPilot(false)\n  565 |       // Load new brand data\n  566 |       loadDetail(activeBrand.id)\n\n/Users/alextian/Documents/Claude/Projects/AI Staff/amc-kanban/src/components/dashboard/DashboardHome.tsx:582:24\n  580 |\n  581 |   // ── Local UI state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n> 582 |   const [dismissedIds, setDismissedIds] = useState<Set<string>>(new Set())\n      |                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `setDismissedIds` is declared here\n  583 |   const [autoPilot, setAutoPilot] = useState(false)\n  584 |   const [showAddAccount, setShowAddAccount] = useState(false)\n  585 |   const [showSettings, setShowSettings] = useState(false)","line":563,"column":7,"nodeType":null,"endLine":563,"endColumn":22},{"ruleId":"react-hooks/immutability","severity":2,"message":"Error: Cannot access variable before it is declared\n\n`setAutoPilot` is accessed before it is declared, which prevents the earlier access from updating when this value changes over time.\n\n/Users/alextian/Documents/Claude/Projects/AI Staff/amc-kanban/src/components/dashboard/DashboardHome.tsx:564:7\n  562 |       setBrandAgents([])\n  563 |       setDismissedIds(new Set())\n> 564 |       setAutoPilot(false)\n      |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^ `setAutoPilot` accessed before it is declared\n  565 |       // Load new brand data\n  566 |       loadDetail(activeBrand.id)\n  567 |       loadSettings(activeBrand.id)\n\n/Users/alextian/Documents/Claude/Projects/AI Staff/amc-kanban/src/components/dashboard/DashboardHome.tsx:583:21\n  581 |   // ── Local UI state ─────────────